## Goal
QA coverage for the iCloud "offloaded" handling (DEV-45): confirm `Offloaded` gives no false positives on real BSD file flags, and that the offloaded link-routing path runs handlers in the right order and writes a correct log line.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
Two test-only files were added, with no production code changes.

- `internal/sync/offload_darwin_test.go` (darwin build tag) runs the real `Offloaded` check on files in a temp dir, which iCloud never manages. It covers regular and empty files, other BSD flags (`UF_IMMUTABLE`, `UF_HIDDEN`, `UF_NODUMP` and combinations), symlinks, directories, missing files, and a directory or a different file named like an `.icloud` placeholder. `SF_DATALESS` can only be set by the kernel or File Provider, so `platformDataless` is checked on a synthetic `Stat_t` instead.
- `cmd/portero/offload_qa_test.go` checks, for `routeLinkWith` and `openUI`, that the browser opens before the download starts. It also checks that the log line has five tab-separated columns, with `-` when there is no opener. An open error is returned while the download still starts. A non-URL is refused before anything opens or downloads.

Temp-dir files and a synthetic `Stat_t` keep the tests deterministic and independent of a real iCloud account.

